Source: hoserva
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Hoserva <releases@hoserva.dev>
# Only debhelper is a real Build-Depends: the Go and Node toolchains this
# build also needs come from the CI job's own setup steps (go.mod,
# web/.nvmrc pin exact versions stricter than anything Debian 13 ships),
# not from apt — the same posture ci.yml's own cross-compile job already
# takes for Go. debian/rules forces --buildsystem=none so debhelper never
# tries to drive that build itself from the presence of go.mod.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://hoserva.dev
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: hoserva
Architecture: any
# S8 (doc 08 §8, Q7) confirmed Debian 13's mergerfs 2.40.2 and SnapRAID
# 12.4 against every option and create policy Hoserva's own default
# configuration uses; no upper bound, so a Debian security update to
# either package is never blocked by this dependency (Q7).
Depends: adduser, mergerfs (>= 2.40.2), snapraid (>= 12.4), ${misc:Depends}
# Optional off-box backup destinations (Q41, doc 10 §1) — local
# destinations work without it, and the UI offers the install command
# the first time a remote one is configured. Docker is deliberately not
# a dependency here (D8): it is a prerequisite the user installs from
# Docker's own repository, checked and reported by `hoservad`/`hoserva
# doctor`, not something this package pulls in.
Recommends: rclone
Description: Home server management for mixed-size disks
 Hoserva is a management layer over mergerfs and SnapRAID: a daemon, CLI
 and web UI that pool mismatched drives behind one mergerfs mount, keep
 SnapRAID parity in sync on a schedule, and refuse to sync past a
 tripped fill-threshold guard. It generates mergerfs/SnapRAID
 configuration from its own database and drives both tools rather than
 reimplementing either.
 .
 This package installs hoservad (the daemon — it runs as root because it
 partitions disks and manages mounts) as the hoserva.service systemd
 unit, and the hoserva CLI. Docker Engine is a separate prerequisite,
 installed from Docker's own repository, needed only for the Apps
 section.
